{#
    The page visitors get while the site is in maintenance, with the 503 status and Retry-After. It stands alone: it
    extends no layout of the application, which may need what the maintenance took away. Variables: maintenance, the
    MaintenanceState.
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <title>Under maintenance</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 40rem; margin: 4rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; text-align: center; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <main>
        <h1>Under maintenance</h1>
        <p>The site is being improved. Please come back in {{ (maintenance.retryAfterSeconds / 60)|round(0, 'ceil') }} minutes.</p>
    </main>
</body>
</html>
